    "final_message": "The red acceptance test is written and committed (2251b83). `scripts/verify story-drafting` passes tessercheck with zero findings and `mypy --strict`. It also passes the non-root tests and the host and Restate registration, then fails at the root tier's pytest step, as intended.\n\n**Test**\n- File: `<repo>/story-drafting/tests/test_acceptance.py`\n- Name: `TestSubmittingAJtbd::test_a_just_submitted_jtbd_is_drafting`\n\n**Spec** (`<repo>/.baseline-runs/red-v9-sonnet-high/spec.toml`)\n- App `story_drafting`, context `drafting`, aggregate `Jtbd` with identity `jtbd_id`.\n- The aggregate's fields are `situation`, `motivation` and `outcome`, the three clauses of a JTBD. It has no status field.\n- Client operations are `submit_jtbd` (write) and `check_status` (read).\n- The orchestrator operation is `draft_stories`, with `calling_mode = \"start\"` (chosen because the workflow will later wait on a person). The action is `record_jtbd`, the repository operations are `save_jtbd` and `load_jtbd`, and the collection is `jtbds`.\n- Storage is `memory` and the host is `http`.\n\n**What the test does**\n1. It POSTs a JTBD to `/jtbds` through the served host and expects 201 with a `jtbd_id`.\n2. It retries `GET /jtbds/{jtbd_id}` until it answers 200, for up to 30 seconds. The generated test already did this because the calling mode is `start`.\n3. It asserts the submit answered 201 and the read 200.\n4. It asserts the read answers the same `jtbd_id` and `situation`.\n5. It asserts the then: `check_status.get(\"status\") == \"drafting\"`.\n\n**Exact failure** (after the submit and the read both succeed):\n`tests/test_acceptance.py:47: AssertionError: assert None == 'drafting'`. The read answers only `jtbd_id`, `situation`, `motivation` and `outcome`.\n\nThe log is at `<repo>/.baseline-runs/red-v9-sonnet-high/verify.log`."
  },
